### Description

This PR adds the ability to sample writeable textures in compute/pixel shaders, by adding a new `Transition` API to `ComputeContext` that allows consumers to temporarily change the state of a writeable texture to be readonly, and then an `AsReadOnly()` API to get a readonly wrapper for a texture (ie. an `IReadOnlyTexture2D<TPixel>`), which can then be used in a shader. This wrapper will expose all APIs for that interface, including those to sample the texture (ie. `float` indexers).

This PR also fixes a number of discovered bugs (eg. sampling indexers for `IReadOnlyTexture3D<TPixel>`).

### API breakdown

```diff
 namespace ComputeSharp;

+public enum ResourceState
+{
+    ReadOnly,
+    ReadWrite
+}

 public sealed class ReadWriteTexture2D<T, TPixel>
 {
+    public IReadOnlyTexture2D<TPixel> AsReadOnly();
 }

 public sealed class ReadWriteTexture3D<T, TPixel>
 {
+    public IReadOnlyTexture3D<TPixel> AsReadOnly();
 }

 public static class ComputeContextExtensions
 {
+    public static void Transition<T, TPixel>(this in ComputeContext context, ReadWriteTexture2D<T, TPixel> texture, ResourceState resourceState) where T : unmanaged, IPixel<T, TPixel> where TPixel : unmanaged;
+    public static void Transition<T, TPixel>(this in ComputeContext context, ReadWriteTexture3D<T, TPixel> texture, ResourceState resourceState) where T : unmanaged, IPixel<T, TPixel> where TPixel : unmanaged;
 }
```

### Example usage

```csharp
using (var context = device.Get().CreateComputeContext())
{
    context.Transition(source, ResourceState.ReadOnly);
    context.ForEach(destination, new LinearSamplingPixelShader(source.AsReadOnly()));
    context.Transition(source, ResourceState.ReadWrite);
}
```
